{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nThe `COMMITS` event and `attach_commits` reducer exist (`rebar.attach_commits`, `src/rebar/_lib_writes.py:697`, re-exported from `src/rebar/__init__.py`), used by code-review. Missing: an author-facing repair surface for a botched `rebar-ticket:` trailer, plus a consumer. Approved design (b902-18af-14ed-4da1): expose retroactive commit linking on CLI + library + MCP, document it, then add a deterministic close-gate check that linked commits' diffs match the recorded `file_impact`. OUT of scope: linked commits as a completion-verifier diff basis (they may be incomplete; CV already prefetches from `file_impact`).\n\n## Plan\n\n1. **Shared DET module** `src/rebar/_engine_support/commit_impact.py` (new, ~120 LOC): (a) `invalid_commit_shas(shas, repo_root)` via `git rev-parse --verify <sha>^{commit}`; (b) the step-4 path matchers, including `glob_match` — the `**/`-aware semantics (`fnmatch(p,g) or (g.startswith(\"**/\") and fnmatch(p,g[3:]))`) from `src/rebar/llm/prompting/prompts.py:746`. Its ONLY true mirror is `src/rebar/llm/code_review/registry.py:242`; `src/rebar/grounding/oracle.py:316` uses PLAIN `fnmatch`, is NOT a copy, and is left untouched. The DET path must not import `rebar.llm` (optional `[agents]` extra), so the helper is hoisted here and BOTH real copies (`prompts._glob_match`, `registry._glob_match`) become thin delegating wrappers — one implementation.\n\n2. **CLI verb** `rebar attach-commits <ticket> <sha>...` wrapping the seam. Add to `_WRITES_FULL` in `src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py`; add a variadic handler (N SHAs) to `_ARGV_REGISTRY` in `src/rebar/_commands/__init__.py`; ship pinned help `src/rebar/_cli/help/attach-commits.txt` + the `overview.txt` line (golden-pinned; `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py` requires it). Thin body in `src/rebar/_commands/attach_commits.py`.\n\n3. **Validation in the SEAM, not the CLI**, so all three surfaces inherit it: `rebar.attach_commits` calls `commit_impact.invalid_commit_shas` before appending. **ALL-OR-NOTHING** — the batch is validated first; if any SHA fails, NO `COMMITS` event is recorded and the call raises naming every offender. Union-add unchanged. Library: `rebar.attach_commits` is already re-exported — confirm and document. MCP: register `attach_commits` in `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py` with an `AttachCommitsResultOut` outputSchema in `src/rebar/_mcp_models.py`, per the existing write-tool pattern (`mcp_server.py` only assembles registrars).\n\n4. **DET close check** in the existing completion precheck `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py` — the module that today raises \"cannot confirm the work landed\" (there is no `src/rebar/workflow/close_gate.py`). Discovery unions the two existing sources: (i) `state.commits` from COMMITS events; (ii) the precheck's referencing-commit scan (`_referencing_commit_exists`, `close_precheck.py:186` — commits reachable from HEAD with a `rebar-ticket:` trailer or leading `<id>:` subject for the ticket or any transitive descendant). It returns only a bool, so it becomes a SHA-returning `_referencing_commits(...)` with `_referencing_commit_exists` kept as a thin wrapper — the documented monkeypatch target and its call sites unchanged. For each commit, `git show --name-only` gives changed paths; a path neither covered by `file_impact` nor matched by this check's OWN exemption globs (`tests/**`, `docs/**`, `**/*.md`, `CHANGELOG.md` — owned here, not inherited) is a deterministic BLOCK naming the commit and paths. Matching (via step 1, not re-derived): normalized repo-relative POSIX paths; a `file_impact` entry matches on exact equality, or as a directory prefix when it ends with `/` or names an existing directory; exemptions use `**/`-aware `glob_match`. No substring matching. No LLM.\n\n   **Merge commits are SKIPPED:** `git show --name-only` emits a combined diff (usually an empty path list) for a merge, so reading it as \"no paths\" would silently pass; a merge authors no change of its own (content arrives via its parents), so it is skipped explicitly. **Git errors, asymmetric by source:** a source-(ii) commit is local by construction, so a `git show` failure FAILS CLOSED (block, naming the SHA). A source-(i) SHA may legitimately be absent locally (another clone, or unfetched), so it is SKIPPED — blocking a foreign SHA would false-positive on a surface built to record commits.\n\n   **Scope symmetry.** Source-(ii) credits commits for the ticket OR any transitive descendant (`accepted_ids`, `close_precheck.py:361`), but `field_reads.file_impact` (`field_reads.py:36`) reads only THIS ticket's — reusing it would false-BLOCK a parent declaring `file_impact` when children's commits touch child-owned paths. So the check compares against the UNION of `file_impact` over the SAME id set discovery uses, making both scopes match by construction.\n\n   A ticket with no discovered commits keeps today's behavior. The check is skipped when the union is empty.\n\n5. **Remedy for a legitimate block:** the message names the offending paths and says to declare them via `rebar set-file-impact <ticket> …`, after which close proceeds; `--force=\"<reason>\"` stays the break-glass.\n\n6. **Docs.** BOTH `docs/cli-reference.md` (`scripts/gen_cli_reference.py`) and `docs/mcp-reference.md` (`scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py`) are GENERATED with CI drift gates — they are REGENERATED, never hand-edited; the MCP tool's registrar docstring is what supplies its reference line. The only hand-edited doc is `src/rebar/_guides/commit-ticket-trailer.md`, which names the verb, its use, and the step-5 remedy.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\nUnless noted, \"test\" = a case in `tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py`; run `pytest tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py -x`.\n\n- [x] `rebar attach-commits <ticket> <sha>` records a COMMITS event `rebar show` reflects.\n- [x] An invalid SHA is rejected with an error naming it.\n- [x] A batch with any invalid SHA records nothing: `state.commits` identical before/after.\n- [x] MCP exposes `attach_commits` with an outputSchema via the same seam; the tool-inventory test asserts the name is registered.\n- [x] A commit path outside the declared `file_impact` blocks close, the message naming that exact path.\n- [x] A commit whose paths are all declared does not block.\n- [x] Each exemption glob does not block, incl. repo root (`README.md` under `**/*.md`).\n- [x] A parent close does not block on a path declared only in a child's `file_impact`.\n- [x] An unreadable source-(ii) commit fails closed naming the SHA; an unresolvable source-(i) SHA is skipped.\n- [x] A merge commit is skipped, not read as an empty path list (test: merge touching an undeclared path, no block).\n- [x] The DET check imports no `rebar.llm`: `[m for m in sys.modules if m.startswith(\"rebar.llm\")] == []` in a fresh interpreter.\n- [x] `prompts._glob_match` and `registry._glob_match` both delegate to `commit_impact.glob_match`.\n- [x] `_referencing_commit_exists` keeps its bool contract (True/False for matching vs non-matching id sets) while `_referencing_commits` returns SHAs.\n- [x] The commit-trailer guide names `rebar attach-commits` and the `rebar set-file-impact` remedy (test `-k docs_guide`).\n- [x] Both generated docs regenerate clean: `python scripts/gen_cli_reference.py --check` and `python scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py --check` each exit 0, and the regenerated `docs/mcp-reference.md` names `attach_commits`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786529875042766001,"uuid":"56268f2e-0125-4ce8-805f-9ad13463dc7c"}